---
title: "Web Font Diagnostics"
layout: "layouts/_default.njk"
body_class: "page-font-test"
---
{% extends "layouts/_default.njk" %}

{% block content %}
<div class="font-tester" id="font-tester">
  <div class="font-tester__header">
    <h1>Web Font Diagnostics</h1>
    <p class="font-tester__intro">
      This page is your tool for verifying that all web fonts configured in
      <code>vite.config.js</code> are loading correctly. Each card shows a
      side-by-side comparison: the <strong>target font</strong> on top and a
      <strong>system fallback</strong> on the bottom at the same weight and
      style, so you can instantly spot whether the browser is using the real
      font or a generic substitute.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="font-tester__guide">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Target line:</strong> Rendered with
        <code>font-family: '&lt;name&gt;', fallback</code> at the configured
        weight and style — this is what the font <em>should</em> look like.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Fallback line:</strong> Rendered with a standard system
        <code>sans-serif</code> (or <code>monospace</code> for monospaced
        fonts) at the same weight and style, so you can compare against the
        browser default.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Status badge:</strong> JavaScript checks
        <code>document.fonts.check()</code> after all CSS fonts finish
        loading. A green "Loaded" badge means the font is available; a red
        "Failed" badge means the browser fell back to a system font.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="font-tester__grid">
    {% for font in site.fonts %}
      {# Determine a sensible fallback family for comparison #}
      {% set fallbackFamily = "sans-serif" %}
      {% if "Mono" in font.name or "mono" in font.name %}
        {% set fallbackFamily = "monospace" %}
      {% endif %}

      <div
        class="font-test-card"
        data-family="{{ font.name }}"
        data-weight="{{ font.weight }}"
        data-style="{{ font.style }}"
      >
        <div class="font-test-card__header">
          <h3 class="font-test-card__title">{{ font.name }}</h3>
          <div class="font-test-card__meta">
            <span>Weight: {{ font.weight }} &middot; Style: {{ font.style }}</span>
            <span class="font-test-card__status" data-status="pending">Checking&hellip;</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="font-test-card__body">
          {# Line 1 — Target font #}
          <div class="font-test-card__row">
            <span class="font-test-card__label">Target:</span>
            <p
              class="font-test-card__preview font-test-card__preview--target"
              style="font-family: '{{ font.name }}', {{ fallbackFamily }}; font-weight: {{ font.weight }}; font-style: {{ font.style }};"
            >
              {{ font.text }}
            </p>
          </div>

          {# Line 2 — System fallback for comparison #}
          <div class="font-test-card__row">
            <span class="font-test-card__label">Fallback:</span>
            <p
              class="font-test-card__preview font-test-card__preview--fallback"
              style="font-family: {{ fallbackFamily }}; font-weight: {{ font.weight }}; font-style: {{ font.style }};"
            >
              {{ font.text }}
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
